    LLM: 'Game: Bisca. Type: Ace-Ten/Draw. Ranking: A(11)>7(10)>K(4)>J(3)>Q(2)>others(0). No follow-suit in draw phase. Target: 61 points.',
    Player: "Your opponent leads the King of Spades (4 pts). You have the Ace of Spades (11 pts) and the 7 of Hearts (trump, 10 pts). Win it cheaply with the Aceâ€”don't waste a trump on a measly King when the pot is small.",
    objective: 'Win the deal by capturing 61 or more of the 120 card points in tricks. The pack has 120 points in total; the player or team with the majority (61+) wins. Often a match is played as best of seven games.',
    gameplay: 'Phase 1 (Draw Phase): 1. Non-dealer leads. 2. No obligation to follow suitâ€”play any card. 3. Trick is won by highest trump, or highest of led suit if no trump. 4. Winner takes trick, draws a card from stock. Loser draws next. 5. Winner leads next trick. Phase 2 (Final Phase): When stock is empty, players play out remaining cards with normal trick-taking rules.',
    keyRules: [
      'There is NO obligation to follow suit during the draw phase.',
      'Trump cards always beat non-trump cards.',
      'The trump-indicator card is the last card drawn from the stock (taken by the winner of the last draw-phase trick).',
    ],
